---
// Offset vs cursor on a newest-first list. Rows one and two: an offset
// window is a position — a new case on top slides everything down, and
// page 2 serves case 8 a second time. Row three: the cursor anchors to
// the data itself (the red accent), immune to insertions above.
const W = 900, H = 280;
const pitch = 40, cw = 34;
const cx = (i: number) => 220 + i * pitch;
const idsBefore = [12, 11, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3];
const idsAfter = [13, 12, 11, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3];
const rows = [
  { y: 28, ids: idsBefore, dup: -1, isNew: false },
  { y: 108, ids: idsAfter, dup: 8, isNew: true },
  { y: 198, ids: idsAfter, dup: -1, isNew: false },
];
---
<figure class="bep2d">
  <div class="bep2d-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Three rows of case cells, newest first. Row one: page one at offset 0 covers cases 12 down to 8. Row two: a new case 13 lands on top, and page two at offset 5 now covers cases 8 down to 4 — case 8 is served a second time. Row three: a cursor anchored after id 8 covers cases 7 down to 3, nothing repeated, even though case 13 is still there.">
    <text x="20" y="44" class="rl"><tspan data-lang-en>before the insert</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>trước khi có vụ mới</tspan></text>
    <text x="20" y="124" class="rl"><tspan data-lang-en>a new case lands on top</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>thêm một vụ lên đầu</tspan></text>
    <text x="20" y="214" class="rl"><tspan data-lang-en>with a cursor</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>dùng con trỏ</tspan></text>
    {rows.map((r) => (
      <g>
        {r.ids.map((id, i) => (
          <g>
            <rect x={cx(i)} y={r.y} width={cw} height="30" rx="4"
              class={r.y === 198 && i >= 6 ? 'cellr' : r.isNew && i === 0 ? 'celln' : 'cell'} />
            <text x={cx(i) + cw / 2} y={r.y + 19} text-anchor="middle" class={r.isNew && i === 0 ? 'ct n' : 'ct'}>{id}</text>
          </g>
        ))}
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x="237" y="102" text-anchor="middle" class="tag"><tspan data-lang-en>new</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>mới</tspan></text>
    <text x="437" y="102" text-anchor="middle" class="tag"><tspan data-lang-en>seen on page 1</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>đã thấy ở trang 1</tspan></text>
    <rect x={cx(5)} y="108" width={cw} height="30" rx="4" class="celld" />
    <path d="M 218 62 L 218 70 L 416 70 L 416 62" class="br" />
    <text x="317" y="88" text-anchor="middle" class="bl"><tspan data-lang-en>page 1 · offset 0 — cases 12…8</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>trang 1 · offset 0 — vụ 12…8</tspan></text>
    <path d="M 418 142 L 418 150 L 616 150 L 616 142" class="br" />
    <text x="517" y="168" text-anchor="middle" class="bl"><tspan data-lang-en>page 2 · offset 5 — cases 8…4</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>trang 2 · offset 5 — vụ 8…4</tspan></text>
    <path d="M 460 194 L 460 186 L 656 186 L 656 194" class="brr" />
    <polygon points="457,232 450,242 464,242" class="tri" />
    <text x="440" y="262" text-anchor="middle" class="blr"><tspan data-lang-en>cursor after id 8 → next page: cases 7…3, nothing repeated</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>con trỏ sau id 8 → trang sau: vụ 7…3, không lặp vụ nào</tspan></text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Offset windows are positions in a list that moves. A newest-first feed, one new case on top, and page 2 (offset 5) serves case 8 twice — the client sees a duplicate and cannot tell. A cursor holds "start after id 8": insertions above cannot move it, so the next page starts at 7 with nothing repeated. (The demo in this post orders by case_id ascending, so its own offsets are stable — this is the feed ordering, where offsets bite.)</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Cửa sổ offset là vị trí trong một danh sách biết di chuyển. Feed mới-nhất-trên-đầu, thêm một vụ lên đầu, là trang 2 (offset 5) trả vụ 8 đến hai lần — client thấy trùng mà chẳng biết vì sao. Con trỏ giữ "bắt đầu sau id 8": chèn bao nhiêu phía trên cũng không xê dịch, trang sau bắt đầu từ 7, không lặp vụ nào. (Demo trong bài sắp theo case_id tăng dần nên offset của nó ổn — sắp kiểu feed mới-nhất-trên-đầu mới là chỗ offset bắt đầu nói dối.)</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .bep2d { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .bep2d-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .bep2d svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .bep2d text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .bep2d .rl { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); font-size: 13.5px; }
  .bep2d .ct { fill: var(--text-body); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .bep2d .n { font-weight: 700; }
  .bep2d .tag { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11.5px; }
  .bep2d .bl { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .bep2d .blr { fill: var(--red); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .bep2d .cell { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1; }
  .bep2d .celln { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .bep2d .celld { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .bep2d .cellr { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .bep2d .br { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; fill: none; }
  .bep2d .brr { stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.5; fill: none; }
  .bep2d .tri { fill: var(--red); }
  .bep2d figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
